IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc1-s3-6-interpretation.l4 -- Part I (General) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: sections 3.1 to 6.
-- Effect of judicial acts, rules of reading for this Act (value of postal cards and valuable securities, possession, words taken from other
-- Acts, sexual intercourse, proof of service, telecommunication), the Canadian Forces, the presumption of innocence and offences outside Canada.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- HOW A RESULT READS (the rule of 2026-10-29 and the rulings of 2026-11-04, -05 and -12; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md):
--   JUST TRUE   the facts bring the case within the provision, on the text's own words;
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means"; a condition introduced by "if", "where", "when", "while", "until", "unless",
--               "except"; a flat negative: "does not", "shall not", "is not entitled", "no ... shall");
--   NOTHING     not covered: the provision is silent, lists without closing the list, points outside the sources, or limits a grant in
--               its own wording and the case falls outside the limit. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every branch that answers JUST FALSE carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"` and every branch that
-- answers NOTHING carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.

§ `Section 3.1 -- Effect of judicial acts`

-- 3.1 (1): anything done by a court, justice or judge is effective from the moment it is done, whether or not reduced to writing.
-- src:276 | Effect of judicial acts
-- src:277 | 3.1 (1) Unless otherwise provided or ordered, anything done by a court, justice or judge is effective from the moment it is done, whether or not it is reduced to writing.
@ref s 3.1(1) (src:276-277)
GIVEN `it was done by a court, justice or judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is otherwise provided or ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3.1(1) what was done is effective from the moment it is done` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it was done by a court, justice or judge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "anything done by a court, justice or judge"
        IF `it is otherwise provided or ordered` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless otherwise provided or ordered"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 3.1 (2): if anything is done from the bench by a court, justice or judge and it is reduced to writing, the clerk of the court may sign the writing.
-- src:278 | Clerk of the court
-- src:279 | (2) Unless otherwise provided or ordered, if anything is done from the bench by a court, justice or judge and it is reduced to writing, the clerk of the court may sign the writing.
@ref s 3.1(2) (src:278-279)
GIVEN `it was done from the bench by a court, justice or judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reduced to writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is otherwise provided or ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3.1(2) the clerk of the court may sign the writing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is otherwise provided or ordered` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless otherwise provided or ordered"
        IF NOT (`it was done from the bench by a court, justice or judge` AND `it is reduced to writing`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if anything is done from the bench by a court, justice or judge and it is reduced to writing"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 4 -- Rules of reading for the purposes of this Act`

-- 4 (1): a postal card or stamp referred to in paragraph (c) of the definition property in section 2 is deemed a chattel and equal in value to the postage, rate or duty on its face.
-- src:280 | Postcard a chattel, value
-- src:281 | 4 (1) For the purposes of this Act, a postal card or stamp referred to in paragraph (c) of the definition property in section 2 shall be deemed to be a chattel and to be equal in value to the amount of the postage, rate or duty expressed on its face.
@ref s 4(1) (src:280-281)
GIVEN `it is a postal card or stamp referred to in paragraph (c) of the definition property in section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) the postal card or stamp is deemed to be a chattel` MEANS
    IF `it is a postal card or stamp referred to in paragraph (c) of the definition property in section 2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a postal card or stamp referred to in paragraph (c) of the definition property in section 2"

@ref s 4(1) (src:281-281)
GIVEN `it is a postal card or stamp referred to in paragraph (c) of the definition property in section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the postage, rate or duty expressed on its face, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 4(1) the postal card or stamp is deemed equal in value to the amount expressed on its face` MEANS
    IF `it is a postal card or stamp referred to in paragraph (c) of the definition property in section 2`
    THEN JUST `the amount of the postage, rate or duty expressed on its face, in dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a postal card or stamp referred to in paragraph (c) of the definition property in section 2"

-- 4 (2): the rules for the value of a valuable security where value is material; the paragraphs are those of the definition valuable security in section 2.
-- src:282 | Value of valuable security
-- src:283 | (2) For the purposes of this Act, the following rules apply for the purpose of determining the value of a valuable security where value is material:
-- src:284 | (a) where the valuable security is one mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition valuable security in section 2, the value is the value of the share, interest, deposit or unpaid money, as the case may be, that is secured by the valuable security;
-- src:285 | (b) where the valuable security is one mentioned in paragraph (c) or (d) of the definition valuable security in section 2, the value is the value of the lands, goods, chattel personal or interest in the chattel personal, as the case may be; and
-- src:286 | (c) where the valuable security is one mentioned in paragraph (e) of the definition valuable security in section 2, the value is the amount of money that has been paid.
@ref s 4(2) (src:282-286)
DECLARE `s 4(2) paragraph of the definition valuable security` IS ONE OF
    `s 4(2)(a) paragraph (a) of the definition valuable security`   -- an order, exchequer acquittance or other security entitling to a share, interest or deposit
    `s 4(2)(a) paragraph (b) of the definition valuable security`   -- a debenture, deed, bond, bill, note, warrant, order or other security for money
    `s 4(2)(b) paragraph (c) of the definition valuable security`   -- a document of title to lands or goods
    `s 4(2)(b) paragraph (d) of the definition valuable security`   -- a stamp or writing securing or evidencing title to a chattel personal
    `s 4(2)(c) paragraph (e) of the definition valuable security`   -- a release, receipt, discharge or other instrument evidencing payment of money
    `s 4(2) none of those paragraphs`

@ref s 4(2) (src:282-286)
GIVEN paragraph IS A `s 4(2) paragraph of the definition valuable security`
      `the value of the share, interest, deposit or unpaid money secured, as the case may be, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the lands, goods, chattel personal or interest in the chattel personal, as the case may be, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of money that has been paid, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 4(2) the value of the valuable security, where value is material` MEANS
    CONSIDER paragraph
    WHEN `s 4(2)(a) paragraph (a) of the definition valuable security` THEN JUST `the value of the share, interest, deposit or unpaid money secured, as the case may be, in dollars`
    WHEN `s 4(2)(a) paragraph (b) of the definition valuable security` THEN JUST `the value of the share, interest, deposit or unpaid money secured, as the case may be, in dollars`
    WHEN `s 4(2)(b) paragraph (c) of the definition valuable security` THEN JUST `the value of the lands, goods, chattel personal or interest in the chattel personal, as the case may be, in dollars`
    WHEN `s 4(2)(b) paragraph (d) of the definition valuable security` THEN JUST `the value of the lands, goods, chattel personal or interest in the chattel personal, as the case may be, in dollars`
    WHEN `s 4(2)(c) paragraph (e) of the definition valuable security` THEN JUST `the amount of money that has been paid, in dollars`
    WHEN `s 4(2) none of those paragraphs` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the rules name only paragraphs (a) to (e) of the definition valuable security in section 2

-- 4 (3): possession.
-- src:287 | Possession
-- src:288 | (3) For the purposes of this Act,
-- src:289 | (a) a person has anything in possession when he has it in his personal possession or knowingly
-- src:290 | (i) has it in the actual possession or custody of another person, or
-- src:291 | (ii) has it in any place, whether or not that place belongs to or is occupied by him, for the use or benefit of himself or of another person; and
-- src:292 | (b) where one of two or more persons, with the knowledge and consent of the rest, has anything in his custody or possession, it shall be deemed to be in the custody and possession of each and all of them.
@ref s 4(3)(a) (src:287-292)
GIVEN `the person has it in his personal possession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly has it in the actual possession or custody of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly has it in any place, whether or not that place belongs to or is occupied by him, for the use or benefit of himself or of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(3)(a) the person has the thing in possession` MEANS
    IF `the person has it in his personal possession`
       OR `the person knowingly has it in the actual possession or custody of another person`
       OR `the person knowingly has it in any place, whether or not that place belongs to or is occupied by him, for the use or benefit of himself or of another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has anything in possession when he has it in his personal possession or knowingly"

@ref s 4(3)(b) (src:292-292)
GIVEN `one of two or more persons has the thing in his custody or possession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he does so with the knowledge and consent of the rest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(3)(b) the thing is deemed to be in the custody and possession of each and all of them` MEANS
    IF `one of two or more persons has the thing in his custody or possession` AND `he does so with the knowledge and consent of the rest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where one of two or more persons, with the knowledge and consent of the rest, has anything in his custody or possession"

-- 4 (4): words and expressions of an offence that relates to a subject dealt with in another Act have, subject to this Act, the meaning assigned in that other Act.
-- src:293 | Expressions taken from other Acts
-- src:294 | (4) Where an offence that is dealt with in this Act relates to a subject that is dealt with in another Act, the words and expressions used in this Act with respect to that offence have, subject to this Act, the meaning assigned to them in that other Act.
@ref s 4(4) (src:293-294)
GIVEN `the offence is dealt with in this Act and relates to a subject that is dealt with in another Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act itself assigns the word or expression a meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(4) the word or expression has the meaning assigned to it in the other Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence is dealt with in this Act and relates to a subject that is dealt with in another Act` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence that is dealt with in this Act relates to a subject that is dealt with in another Act"
        IF `this Act itself assigns the word or expression a meaning` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to this Act"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 4 (5): sexual intercourse is complete on penetration to even the slightest degree, notwithstanding that seed is not emitted.
-- src:295 | Sexual intercourse
-- src:296 | (5) For the purposes of this Act, sexual intercourse is complete on penetration to even the slightest degree, notwithstanding that seed is not emitted.
@ref s 4(5) (src:295-296)
GIVEN `there has been penetration, to even the slightest degree` IS A BOOLEAN
      `seed has been emitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(5) sexual intercourse is complete` MEANS
    IF `there has been penetration, to even the slightest degree`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- whether or not `seed has been emitted`: "notwithstanding that seed is not emitted"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sexual intercourse is complete on penetration to even the slightest degree"

-- 4 (6): the service of any document and the giving or sending of any notice may be proved (a) by oral evidence under oath, or affidavit or solemn declaration of the person claiming to have served; or (b) for a peace officer, by a signed statement, deemed made under oath.
-- src:297 | Proof of notifications and service of documents
-- src:298 | (6) For the purposes of this Act, the service of any document and the giving or sending of any notice may be proved
-- src:299 | (a) by oral evidence given under oath by, or by the affidavit or solemn declaration of, the person claiming to have served, given or sent it; or
-- src:300 | (b) in the case of a peace officer, by a statement in writing certifying that the document was served or the notice was given or sent by the peace officer, and such a statement is deemed to be a statement made under oath.
@ref s 4(6) (src:297-300)
DECLARE `s 4(6) way of proving service or notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 4(6)(a) oral evidence given under oath by the person claiming to have served, given or sent it`
    `s 4(6)(a) the affidavit or solemn declaration of the person claiming to have served, given or sent it`
    `s 4(6)(b) a statement in writing by a peace officer certifying that the document was served or the notice was given or sent by the peace officer`
    `s 4(6) another way of proof`

@ref s 4(6) (src:297-300)
GIVEN way IS A `s 4(6) way of proving service or notice`
      `s 2 peace officer: the person who makes the statement is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(6) the service or notice may be proved in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `s 4(6)(a) oral evidence given under oath by the person claiming to have served, given or sent it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4(6)(a) the affidavit or solemn declaration of the person claiming to have served, given or sent it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 4(6)(b) a statement in writing by a peace officer certifying that the document was served or the notice was given or sent by the peace officer` THEN
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person who makes the statement is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a peace officer" (and, if s 2 peace officer is itself NOTHING, points outside the text)
    WHEN `s 4(6) another way of proof` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be proved" names two ways and does not say "only"

@ref s 4(6)(b) (src:300-300)
GIVEN `the statement is the statement in writing of a peace officer under paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(6)(b) the statement is deemed to be a statement made under oath` MEANS
    IF `the statement is the statement in writing of a peace officer under paragraph (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such a statement is deemed to be a statement made under oath"

-- 4 (6.1): despite (6), service of documents may be proved in accordance with the laws of a province relating to offences created by the laws of that province.
-- src:301 | Proof of service in accordance with provincial laws
-- src:302 | (6.1) Despite subsection (6), the service of documents may be proved in accordance with the laws of a province relating to offences created by the laws of that province.
@ref s 4(6.1) (src:301-302)
GIVEN `the offence is one created by the laws of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proof is in accordance with the laws of the province relating to offences created by its laws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(6.1) the service of documents may be proved in accordance with the laws of the province` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence is one created by the laws of a province` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "relating to offences created by the laws of that province"
        IF NOT `the proof is in accordance with the laws of the province relating to offences created by its laws` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be proved in accordance with the laws of a province"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 4 (7): despite (6) or (6.1), the court may require the person who appears to have signed to appear for examination or cross-examination.
-- src:303 | Attendance for examination
-- src:304 | (7) Despite subsection (6) or (6.1), the court may require the person who appears to have signed an affidavit, a solemn declaration or a statement in accordance with that subsection to appear before it for examination or cross-examination in respect of the issue of proof of service or of the giving or sending of any notice.
@ref s 4(7) (src:303-304)
GIVEN `the person appears to have signed an affidavit, a solemn declaration or a statement in accordance with subsection (6) or (6.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the examination or cross-examination is in respect of the issue of proof of service or of the giving or sending of any notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(7) the court may require the person to appear before it for examination or cross-examination` MEANS
    IF `the person appears to have signed an affidavit, a solemn declaration or a statement in accordance with subsection (6) or (6.1)`
       AND `the examination or cross-examination is in respect of the issue of proof of service or of the giving or sending of any notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of the issue of proof of service or of the giving or sending of any notice"

-- 4 (8): for greater certainty, if the elements of an offence contain an explicit or implicit element of communication without specifying the means, the communication may also be made by a means of telecommunication.
-- src:305 | Means of telecommunication
-- src:306 | (8) For greater certainty, for the purposes of this Act, if the elements of an offence contain an explicit or implicit element of communication without specifying the means of communication, the communication may also be made by a means of telecommunication.
@ref s 4(8) (src:305-306)
GIVEN `the elements of the offence contain an explicit or implicit element of communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the elements specify the means of communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(8) the communication may also be made by a means of telecommunication` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the elements of the offence contain an explicit or implicit element of communication` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "contain an explicit or implicit element of communication"
        IF `the elements specify the means of communication` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without specifying the means of communication"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 5 -- Canadian Forces not affected`

-- 5: nothing in this Act affects any law relating to the government of the Canadian Forces.
-- src:307 | Canadian Forces not affected
-- src:308 | 5 Nothing in this Act affects any law relating to the government of the Canadian Forces.
@ref s 5 (src:307-308)
GIVEN `the law relates to the government of the Canadian Forces` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5 this Act affects the law` MEANS
    IF `the law relates to the government of the Canadian Forces`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Act affects any law relating to the government of the Canadian Forces."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 5 speaks only of laws relating to the government of the Canadian Forces

§ `Section 6 -- Presumption of innocence`

-- 6 (1): where an enactment creates an offence and authorizes a punishment, (a) a person is deemed not guilty until convicted or discharged under section 730; (b) is not liable to any punishment other than the one prescribed.
-- src:309 | Presumption of innocence
-- src:310 | 6 (1) Where an enactment creates an offence and authorizes a punishment to be imposed in respect of that offence,
-- src:311 | (a) a person shall be deemed not to be guilty of the offence until he is convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence; and
-- src:312 | (b) a person who is convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence is not liable to any punishment in respect thereof other than the punishment prescribed by this Act or by the enactment that creates the offence.
@ref s 6(1)(a) (src:309-312)
GIVEN `an enactment creates the offence and authorizes a punishment to be imposed in respect of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been discharged under section 730 of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(1)(a) the person is deemed not to be guilty of the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an enactment creates the offence and authorizes a punishment to be imposed in respect of it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an enactment creates an offence and authorizes a punishment to be imposed in respect of that offence"
        IF `the person has been convicted of the offence` OR `the person has been discharged under section 730 of the offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until he is convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 6(1)(b) (src:312-312)
GIVEN `an enactment creates the offence and authorizes a punishment to be imposed in respect of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the punishment is the punishment prescribed by this Act or by the enactment that creates the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(1)(b) the person is liable to the punishment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an enactment creates the offence and authorizes a punishment to be imposed in respect of it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an enactment creates an offence and authorizes a punishment to be imposed in respect of that offence"
        IF NOT `the person is convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who is convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence"
        IF `the punishment is the punishment prescribed by this Act or by the enactment that creates the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph only excludes other punishments; it does not itself make the person liable to the prescribed one
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not liable to any punishment in respect thereof other than the punishment prescribed by this Act or by the enactment that creates the offence"

-- 6 (2): subject to this Act or any other Act of Parliament, no person shall be convicted or discharged under section 730 of an offence committed outside Canada.
-- src:313 | Offences outside Canada
-- src:314 | (2) Subject to this Act or any other Act of Parliament, no person shall be convicted or discharged under section 730 of an offence committed outside Canada.
@ref s 6(2) (src:313-314)
GIVEN `the offence was committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act or another Act of Parliament provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(2) conviction or discharge under section 730 is barred because the offence was committed outside Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence was committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence committed outside Canada"
        IF `this Act or another Act of Parliament provides otherwise` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to this Act or any other Act of Parliament"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 6 (3): enactment means (a) an Act of Parliament, or (b) an Act of a provincial legislature that creates an offence to which Part XXVII applies, or any regulation made thereunder.
-- src:315 | Definition of enactment
-- src:316 | (3) In this section, enactment means
-- src:317 | (a) an Act of Parliament, or
-- src:318 | (b) an Act of the legislature of a province that creates an offence to which Part XXVII applies,
-- src:319 | or any regulation made thereunder.
@ref s 6(3) (src:315-319)
GIVEN `it is an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an Act of the legislature of a province that creates an offence to which Part XXVII applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a regulation made under such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(3) the instrument is an enactment` MEANS
    IF `it is an Act of Parliament` OR `it is an Act of the legislature of a province that creates an offence to which Part XXVII applies` OR `it is a regulation made under such an Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section, enactment means"
